# Drafted by Gemini (R18 forest2), edited.

~ common
set hb_f5_seen
Narrator: Hollowed tree roots yawn around a muddy green where twelve satyrs drum in the drifting spores. A keeper chants low in the old tongue at their middle.
* Search a dwelling -> dwelling
* Watch the circle -> common_watch
* Leave -> END

~ common_watch
Narrator: The drummers sway with shut eyes, deaf to everything save their wet, steady beat. The only path deeper into the wood leads right past their heels.
-> common

~ dwelling
Narrator: Inside the rotten trunk lie mouldy straw, antler idols, gourd rattles, and cracked prayer rings. A suit of bark and hide hangs beside the door.
* [Investigation DC 12] Search the dwelling -> dwelling_ok | dwelling_fail
* Try on the druid clothes -> garb
* Leave -> common

~ dwelling_ok
Narrator: Tucked beneath a pile of damp pelts, your fingers close around a stoppered clay jar smelling cleanly of clover and beeswax.
give restorative_ointment
-> common

~ dwelling_fail
Narrator: You turn over wet bedding and split gourds for a solid ten minutes, finding nothing but a lungful of warm grey dust.
time +10
set hb_blight += 1
-> common

~ garb
Narrator: The bark and cured hide are clammy against the skin and reek of sour sap, though in this dim light one of you might pass for a local.
give druid_rot_garb
set hb_garb_taken
-> common

~ ravine
Narrator: A narrow cleft winds ahead, floored in slick jelly and roofed with webbing where swollen sap-bulbs hang like yellow lanterns.
* [Nature DC 15] Ask what the bulbs are -> ravine_ok | ravine_plain
* Cross single file without touching the walls -> cross
* Run across -> cross_dash
* Cut a bulb down from afar -> ravine_cut
* Leave -> END

~ ravine_ok
Narrator: Those bladders are taut as boils and tethered to every root along the walls. Brush a single strand and the whole ceiling will spill what it is nursing.
-> ravine

~ ravine_plain
Narrator: They look heavy, wet, and none too friendly, though what they hold is anyone's guess.
-> ravine

~ cross
check Acrobatics DC 17 -> cross_ok | cross_bad

~ cross_ok
Narrator: You place each boot with dry-mouthed care across the slime. Overhead, the fat yellow bladders never so much as tremble.
set hb_ravine_done
-> END

~ cross_bad
Narrator: A heel slips in the grease, a root-line twangs, and the heavy sacs overhead split with a wet sigh.
set hb_ravine_done
combat hb_jellies

~ cross_dash
Narrator: Heavy boots set the root-walls shuddering, and overhead the swollen sacs split open with a wet sigh.
set hb_ravine_done
combat hb_jellies

~ ravine_cut
Narrator: The severed bladder bursts across the web, and its neighbours split in answer, slopping thick yellow mire into the gorge.
set hb_ravine_done
combat hb_jellies

~ pool
Narrator: Amidst the stinking mud pits and green scum lies one basin of water as clear as well-glass. Something pale and round glints on the bottom.
* [Arcana DC 14] Study the clear pool -> pool_ok | pool_plain
* Immerse in the clear pool -> dip
* Leave -> END

~ pool_ok
Narrator: Old spring-grace still lingers in the basin, hungry to drink the rot from living flesh. Each washing will cloud the water darker, and greed will sour it for good.
-> pool

~ pool_plain
Narrator: The water smells sweet and cold against the surrounding mire, though why the rot spares it is hard to say.
-> pool

~ dip
set hb_pool_uses += 1
if flag.hb_pool_uses <= 1
-> dip_clean
elif flag.hb_pool_uses == 2
check Nature DC 10 -> dip_clean | dip_foul
elif flag.hb_pool_uses == 3
check Nature DC 13 -> dip_clean | dip_foul
else
check Nature DC 16 -> dip_clean | dip_foul
endif

~ dip_clean
if flag.hb_blight > 0
set hb_blight -= 1
endif
Narrator: Cold water bites through the fever in your veins, drawing a grey film from your skin that leaves the basin a shade darker.
-> pool

~ dip_foul
Narrator: The water turns pitch-black with a belch of marsh gas, and three dripping heaps of root and carrion heave themselves out of the mud.
set hb_pool_fouled
combat hb_mounds

~ pool_drained
Narrator: With the muck-beasts felled, the basin sucks dry into the mud, leaving a pale bone ring carved with woodland script upon the stones.
-> END

~ gloom_start
Narrator: Pale-green fungal stalks tower round a massive gnarled tree-man draped in red corpse-blooms, its hollow trunk groaning like split timber.
gloomwood [angry]: Turn back, warm meat. Only what is promised to the mould may walk the inner stand.
* [Persuasion DC 17] Talk it down -> gloom_try2 | gloom_fail
* [Intimidation DC 17] Face it down -> gloom_try2 | gloom_fail
* [Performance DC 17] Sing it a calm -> gloom_try2 | gloom_fail
* [if flag.hb_knows_greenwood] Carve the name of the Greenwood into its trunk -> gloom_carve
* Fight it -> gloom_fight
* Leave -> END

~ gloom_try2
Narrator: The great boughs creak to a halt, and a shower of damp petals drifts from its shoulders.
gloomwood [weary]: Strange voices under the cap-light. Speak plain before my roots remember their anger.
* [Persuasion DC 17] Ask it to let you pass -> gloom_blessing | gloom_fail2
* Fight it -> gloom_fight

~ gloom_fail
gloomwood [angry]: Noise and dry breath. The soil wants your marrow, not your words.
-> gloom_start

~ gloom_fail2
gloomwood [angry]: Enough chatter. Lie down in the mulch and be still.
-> gloom_start

~ gloom_blessing
gloomwood [neutral]: Breathe deep of the bloom, then. Carry our gift in your lungs, and the grove will part for you.
set hb_gloomwood_talked_down
set hb_blight += 4
set hb_grove_done
Narrator: A hot, sweet cloud puffs from the red flowers into your throats, and the pale stalks draw aside to open a path.
-> hartsblight/gorthos:parley3

~ gloom_carve
Narrator: Your blade scores the old woodland name into the punky bark, and a long shudder takes the giant, dulling the swing of its heavy limbs.
set hb_gloom_carved
combat hb_gloomwood

~ gloom_fight
combat hb_gloomwood

~ flower
Narrator: Inside a wilted corpse-flower rests a leathery seed-pod the size of a fist, warm and faintly twitching to the touch.
* Take the pod -> flower_take
* Leave -> END

~ flower_take
Narrator: You tuck the warm pod into your pack, where it gives a muffled thump like a sleeping heart that will wake by tomorrow.
give devils_glove_pod
set hb_pod_taken
-> END
